  "equipment_type": "Fan coil unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Four-pipe fan coil units with separate cooling and heating valves on the Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller 550-496PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6645 runs a fan coil unit with separate chilled and hot water valves on a Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller over BACnet MS/TP. The cooling and heating loops modulate VLV 1 and VLV 2, and the fan either runs all day or cycles with valve demand (CYCLE FAN). Heat/cool switchover is automatic, based on loop outputs and the switchover deadband, limit and time.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "If the application drives a damper instead of a cooling valve, the fan sequence does not apply."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Unit Conditioner - Fan Coil Unit Cooling and Heating, Application 6645, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1172",
